WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.210
- So first of all,
thank you for letting me

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.650
be your neighbor and bring you some cake.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:06.320
- Thank you so much.
- It's a really good cake.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.150
- I took the Bundt home.
- Yes.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.510
- Yeah, I put ice cream on top of it.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.343
(audience gasps)
- Oh my gosh

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:12.750
you're my husband.
- It's too much.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:13.970
That was too much sweetness.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:14.803
I shoulda just left it

00:00:14.803 --> 00:00:15.762
at the Bundt.
- Okay you're not my husband.

00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:16.880
(laughing)
He can totally.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.760
He literally will bring
a mixing bowl full.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.020
He's the most fit-looking,
skinny individual.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.308
I wanna cut him in his sleep.

00:00:24.308 --> 00:00:26.272
(laughing)

00:00:26.272 --> 00:00:28.180
- So I am like your husband.
- No, he eats

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.440
whatever he wants.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.691
It's always a vat of ice cream.

00:00:31.691 --> 00:00:33.695
- Have you gotten a Bundt yet?
- No I didn't get

00:00:33.695 --> 00:00:34.910
a Bundt yet.
- Aww why'd you bring

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.191
it up Chris?
- It's okay.

00:00:36.191 --> 00:00:37.400
(laughing)

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.870
- It's because it was for my neighbors

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.340
and you weren't on this lot.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.190
- Well I actually am your neighbor.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.023
- [Kelly] You are kinda my neighbor now.

00:00:42.023 --> 00:00:44.640
- I live so close to here.
- We'll send you a Bundt.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.870
- I'm gonna randomly show
up at your front door

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:47.807
with a Bundt cake and
you're gonna be like,

00:00:47.807 --> 00:00:49.270
"Please go away."
- No, no, I'll be like,

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.793
"Come on, let's have a
glass of wine, Kelly."

00:00:50.793 --> 00:00:52.783
(Kirsten laughs)
- Okay, then I'll hang.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:54.920
So this is something I find interesting

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.310
that I didn't actually
know, you're in a band.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:58.143
- Yeah.
I knew you were always

00:00:58.143 --> 00:01:00.051
kinda cool and rocker 'cause
you always dress cool.

00:01:00.051 --> 00:01:03.150
(audience cheers)
(applause)

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.300
Explain what kind of music.
- Well I'm performing

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.150
under the name Joseph The Spouse.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.810
It's a lot of kind of
country, blues, folk stuff.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.360
- Yes.
- And we just started playing

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.680
around Los Angeles and we'll
have an album forthcoming soon.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.524
- Oh my gosh.
(audience cheers)

00:01:15.524 --> 00:01:18.940
That's amazing.
(applause)

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.150
Is it also because your
co-star's husband, right,

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.190
Mandy's husband?
- Yeah, Taylor Goldsmith,

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.800
the lead singer and songwriter
for a band called Dawes.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.700
- Dawes, yeah, I know Tyalor.
- Yeah.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.660
- Yeah, oh he's amazing.
- And so he and I

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.000
have been writing some songs together.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.870
- Oh that's great, Dawes is great.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.570
- He got the guys together
to come record on the record

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.270
and play live out.
- Oh, so this is gonna be

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.719
a good record.
- I think so.

00:01:37.719 --> 00:01:39.051
- Great.
- I'm excited.

00:01:39.051 --> 00:01:40.183
(audience cheers)
(applause)

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:42.221
- So next time you have
to come back and perform.

00:01:42.221 --> 00:01:43.823
- Absolutely.
- Okay, I want that.

00:01:43.823 --> 00:01:46.520
Well I got a taste of your
singing a few weeks ago.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.140
Just take a look y'all.
(chuckles)

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.740
I wanna know 'cause I know
"This Is Us", the show,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.970
but who are (gasps) you?
- That's right.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:54.870
- Dog or cat person?
- Dog.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.060
- Coffee or tea?
(gasps)

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.151
- Coffee.
- Tea.

00:01:57.151 --> 00:01:59.070
- Yes, Chrissy for the win.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.530
Can you sing your favorite musical note

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:05.353
in your favorite key?
♪ Middle C ♪

00:02:06.202 --> 00:02:08.038
- Can you do it?
- No.

00:02:08.038 --> 00:02:10.705
(laughing)
- No.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.420
- And good.
(laughing)

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.017
(audience cheers)
- That's right.

00:02:21.017 --> 00:02:22.139
- Breath support.
(applause)

00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:25.670
- That's like crazy Celine Dion power.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.100
That breath support is crazy.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.850
You held it forever.
- I held the note

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.641
and it stayed in tune I think.
- No it did

00:02:30.641 --> 00:02:31.900
and it was so long.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.310
I was so tired.
- Not a touch of vibrato.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.946
- That actually is harder,
straight tone with no vibrato.

00:02:37.946 --> 00:02:39.692
- Thank you Kelly Clarkson.
- That's actually way harder.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.528
(audience cheers)

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:43.700
We would've totally
been choir nerd friends.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:44.800
I love us.
- Absolutely.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.290
- Okay, okay.
(Chris chuckles)

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.860
So you dress like a
rocker all the time too.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.930
He showed up with these
really fly sunglasses

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:50.860
that I wish you would've worn out here.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.910
They're so cool, they're
like steampunk a bit.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:53.870
- We'll get 'em out here later.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.530
- They're so cool, but you
always have great fashion.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.363
- Oh thank you,
- We have some pictures

00:02:57.363 --> 00:02:58.196
actually.
- I appreciate it.

00:02:58.196 --> 00:02:59.629
- [Kelly] We have some
pictures that we love.

00:02:59.629 --> 00:03:01.987
(audience cheers)
See, check that out.

00:03:04.088 --> 00:03:05.973
- Exactly.
Where do you even find

00:03:05.973 --> 00:03:07.738
a suit like that?

00:03:07.738 --> 00:03:11.108
(applause)
- The top hat.

00:03:11.108 --> 00:03:13.645
The top hat.
- You say where do you find

00:03:13.645 --> 00:03:17.572
a suit like that, in the
depths of the Internet.

00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:18.420
(Kelly laughs)
- Got it, got it.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:19.650
That makes sense.
(chuckles)

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.180
- I have a favorite one though.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.567
We have a favorite one that I love.

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:23.850
(applause)
- Oh wow.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.730
- I'm gonna be real with you,
I didn't know it was you.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.000
- Well good.
(laughs)

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.249
If you had recognized me from that,

00:03:32.249 --> 00:03:33.340
that'd have been embarrassing.
- No I didn't.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.310
And I would've totally
fanned out even more.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.880
I love "Guardians of the Galaxy".

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.270
Have you seen "Guardians of the Galaxy"?

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:39.960
I know I'm a superhero freak.
- I'm not a huge,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.560
this is so funny coming from me.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:45.320
I'm not a huge superhero fan.
(laughing)

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.710
- Well you like one.
- You like Spiderman.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.803
- You like one super--
- Yeah, I like that one.

00:03:48.803 --> 00:03:50.930
(laughing)
- I like Batman.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.521
- I'm a freak over it and
I love your Taserface.

00:03:53.521 --> 00:03:54.710
- Oh thanks so much.
- That's my favorite

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:55.860
look on you.
- Thank you.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:56.693
(audience applauds)
- It was such

00:03:56.693 --> 00:03:58.020
a great character.
- Thank you.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.480
- So good, you made a villain likable.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.520
(laughs)
- Thanks.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.120
- You made a bad guy good.
- Yeah, he had a dumb face

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.111
and a good heart.
(laughing)

00:04:07.111 --> 00:04:07.944
(hands clap)
- That was great.

00:04:07.944 --> 00:04:09.280
Okay so "This Is Us", Toby.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.683
You now in the show, you're a
new TV dad, you have a baby.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.140
How often do you change the diapers?

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.470
- Well luckily on set I
don't have to change any

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:20.740
of the diapers.
- What?

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:25.740
- And when you're a TV dad,
there's multiple children.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.130
We have triplets.
- Yeah, we had twins

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.203
on the show that I did.

00:04:29.203 --> 00:04:31.457
That looks nothing alike, by the way.

00:04:31.457 --> 00:04:32.840
(audience laughs)
There's one scene

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:33.730
and this other shot,

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.186
I was like, "Oh god, that doesn't."

00:04:35.186 --> 00:04:37.797
(laughing)
Only three babies.

00:04:37.797 --> 00:04:39.780
But they're twins, fraternal.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:44.189
- Because babies can only
work like 13 minutes a day.

00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:46.690
- Yeah, it's true.
- I want that schedule.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.020
- Which is an appropriate amount of work

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.650
to make a baby do.
(laughing)

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.706
- Yeah, agreed.
- 'Cause they didn't sign up.

00:04:52.706 --> 00:04:53.920
- No.
(laughing)

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.910
- No, I don't change any of the diapers.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:57.170
- I think that's unfair.

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:59.624
I wanna see an Instagram
of you changing a diaper.

00:04:59.624 --> 00:05:01.588
(Kelly laughs)
(audience cheers)

00:05:01.588 --> 00:05:03.088
(applause)
- It's not that hard.

00:05:03.088 --> 00:05:05.420
- It seems like calf roping.
- If you have a little boy,

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.330
then you gotta make sure
that diaper goes on quick,

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.890
let's just put it that way.
- Sure.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:11.030
- Have you been peed
on in the face, I have.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:13.513
- I'm sure I have, but I
got that thing on quick.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.525
This is getting maybe a little gross.

00:05:17.525 --> 00:05:19.730
- Don't they have little caps?
- They do, I use,

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:22.750
you know those pads when
you're breast feeding,

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:23.583
those little--
- Yeah.

00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:26.016
- Yeah, I just use those. (hands
clapping) I just have those

00:05:26.016 --> 00:05:27.185
and we slap it on there.

00:05:27.185 --> 00:05:28.580
- We just slapped it on there.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.180
- Slap it on there.
- It can get kinda messy.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.640
I want a messy diaper
that you have to change.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.940
That's the kinda friend I am.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.273
- You know what, I'll do it.
- Okay, okay.

00:05:38.273 --> 00:05:40.090
Kirsten do you sing to your son?

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:41.090
'Cause you're talking
about you know Dawes,

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.280
you know the band, you love music.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.610
- Yes, I do, we sing a
song to him every night,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.943
this Dean Martin song which I keep secret.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:51.290
It's his lullaby song, but
then my mom sings to him

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:53.304
as soon as she walks in
the door, she's like,

00:05:53.304 --> 00:05:54.640
(singing in foreign language)

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.590
She's so loud and then she
just repeats and repeats it

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.720
and repeats it.
- Does she make up songs?

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.990
- Yes with his nickname and she just sings

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.050
and she's so loud.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.840
My grandpa, who he's named after,

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.240
also Howard is his middle name,

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.933
used to sing this song to me.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:09.599
♪ Kikalina Dunst, Kikalina Dunst ♪

00:06:09.599 --> 00:06:10.656
♪ We love you ♪

00:06:10.656 --> 00:06:11.960
♪ Kikalina Dunst, Kikalina ♪

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:13.032
So she does that with

00:06:13.032 --> 00:06:14.659
♪ Enni Hi P, Enni Hi P ♪

00:06:14.659 --> 00:06:16.000
(Chris laughs)
But she's so loud.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.530
- What's Kika?
- Kikalina Dunst.

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:19.697
- Kikalina.
- I don't know, Kikalina.

00:06:19.697 --> 00:06:23.820
- She was smoking something.
(laughing)

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.374
- She's never tried weed.
♪ Kikalina Dunst ♪

00:06:26.374 --> 00:06:28.181
- She was like, "This is
it." ♪ Kikalina Dunst ♪

00:06:28.181 --> 00:06:30.432
♪ Kikalina Dunst ♪

00:06:30.432 --> 00:06:32.232
- She was probably drunk on whiskey.

